implementationPlan.description:
Verification, run once, from your worktree root. Never run npm in the shared checkout (project rail). Run this command exactly; it is also at /mnt/d/moe-scratch/plan-3950184e/gate.sh:

( set -o pipefail; R=$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel) && S=$(mktemp -d /tmp/m3950g.XXXX) && P=packages/moe-daemon && git -C "$R" archive HEAD $P | tar -x -C "$S" && (cd "$R/$P/src" && cp --parents commands/doctorWorktree.ts commands/doctor.test.ts "$S/$P/src") && cd "$S/$P" && echo '{"extends":"./tsconfig.json","include":["src/commands/doctor.test.ts"],"exclude":[]}' > tt.json && env -i HOME="$HOME" PATH="$HOME/.nvm/versions/node/v24.21.0/bin:/usr/bin:/bin" NO_COLOR=1 sh -c 'npm ci >/dev/null 2>&1 && npx tsc --noEmit && npx tsc -p tt.json --noEmit && npx vitest run src/commands/doctor.test.ts src/commands/doctor.bindHost.test.ts --reporter=verbose > ../v.log 2>&1'; E=$?; grep -aE '^ +(Test Files|Tests) ' ../v.log; G=$(grep -acE '✓ src/commands/doctor.test.ts > .* > W([1-9]|10): ' ../v.log); echo "W rows passed: $G/10"; D1=$(grep -E '^\| `worktree control branch` \|' "$R/docs/TROUBLESHOOTING.md" | grep ancestor | grep -c MOE_CONTROL_CHECKOUT_DIVERGED); D2=$(grep -E '^\| `worktree target` \|' "$R/docs/TROUBLESHOOTING.md" | grep 'refs/remotes/origin/' | grep -c MOE_WORKTREE_CREATE_FAILED); echo "doc rows: control=$D1 target=$D2"; [ $E = 0 ] && [ "$G" = 10 ] && [ "$D1" = 1 ] && [ "$D2" = 1 ] || { echo "FAIL $S"; tail -40 ../v.log; exit 1; } )

What it does:
- archives HEAD's packages/moe-daemon to /tmp and overlays your two source files;
- runs npm ci, tsc on the package and tsc on the test file (the package tsconfig excludes tests);
- runs both doctor suites verbose;
- requires vitest exit 0, 'W rows passed: 10/10', and both doc rows.

The architect's dry run of the prototype in a clean clone took about 4 s. It printed 'Test Files 2 passed (2)', 'Tests 84 passed (84)', 'W rows passed: 10/10' and 'doc rows: control=1 target=1', with exit 0.

Submit this command, its exitCode and the output tail as complete_task verification.

Error handling for a red run: the gate prints the ../v.log tail and its snapshot path. Fix the code; never weaken, skip or rename a W row. On a LANDING-RETRY merge, build the snapshot from this worktree's tracked files as the prompt says, and disclose that.
